A Funny Idea
##
I had the idea some time ago of breaking reverse engineers’ decompilers by doing some weird shit with C, namely converting a whole codebase into a single function. By that, I mean packing a whole codebase into a single function,
main()
, which instead of calling other functions to perform some action, every function call is simply replaced by a call to
main()
, and the functionality is achieved somehow in
main()
. At any one time, the callstack would therefore simply be made up of:
main() -> main() -> main() -> main() ...
.
I ended up making a small Python script which achieves both that goal (converting basic single-file C codebases into single-function C codebases), as well as looking at C codebases which have no
main()
function at all. I call it
c-fucker
. Alternatively, think of it as reentrant-as-a-service!
Codebase with only main()
##
